{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/thm-ugb-main","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Theorem","doco:Section"],"label":"thm:ugb-main","kind":"theorem","title":"Freeness of quotient by unital Gröbner--Shirshov basis","uses":["papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/def-admissible-system","papers/unital-groebner-bases/blocks/def-unital-groebner-basis"],"tags":["groebner-basis","freeness","main-result"],"leanRef":"ugb:UGB.Introduction.main_theorem_statement","text":"ugb-main-theorem-statement.md","leanSource":"folio/unital-groebner-bases/introduction/ugb-main-theorem-statement.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"thm:ugb-main\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code> be a commutative algebra with unity. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> be an <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-algebra which is\nfree as an <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-module and without quasi-zeros. Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(B, &#x3C;)</code> be an admissible\nsystem on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> and let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">I</code> be a two-sided ideal of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> with a unital Gröbner--Shirshov\nbasis <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G</code>. Define <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\widetilde{O}(G)</code> to be the free <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-module spanned by the\nmonomials which do not occur as leading monomials of members of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G</code>. Then, as free\n<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">R</code>-modules,</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">A/I \\;\\cong\\; \\widetilde{O}(G) \\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad A \\;=\\; I \\oplus \\widetilde{O}(G).</code></pre>\n","source":"folio/unital-groebner-bases/introduction/ugb-main-theorem-statement.md","leanStatus":"proved","heading":"Theorem","number":"1.2.1"}
